{"id":171,"flavor":[{"games":["Shield","Moon"],"text":"This Pokémon flashes a bright light that blinds its prey. This creates an opening for it to deliver an electrical attack."},{"games":["Sword","HeartGold","LeafGreen","Gold"],"text":"The light it emits is so bright that it can illuminate the sea’s surface from a depth of over three miles."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"It lives far down in the depths of the ocean. It blinds its prey with light, using the moment they’re dazzled to swallow them whole."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"When the bacteria living inside its antennae absorb Lanturn’s bodily fluids, a strong luminescent effect is produced."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"Should you peer into the ocean at night and see a light shining like the stars, that is Lanturn."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Sapphire"],"text":"Lanturn is known to emit light. If you peer down into the dark sea from a ship at night, you can sometimes see this Pokémon’s light rising from the depths where it swims. It gives the sea an appearance of a starlit night."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","Ruby"],"text":"Lanturn is nicknamed “the deep-sea star” for its illuminated antenna. This Pokémon produces light by causing a chemical reaction between bacteria and its bodily fluids inside the antenna."},{"games":["Y","SoulSilver"],"text":"It blinds prey with an intense burst of light. With the prey incapacitated, the Pokémon swallows it in a single gulp."},{"games":["X","White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"Lanturn’s light can shine up from great depths. It is nicknamed “The Deep-Sea Star.”"},{"games":["FireRed","Silver"],"text":"It blinds prey with an intense burst of light, then swallows the immobilized prey in a single gulp."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"The light-emitting orbs on its back are very bright. They are formed from a part of its dorsal fin. This POKéMON illuminates the inky darkness of deep seas."},{"games":["Crystal"],"text":"This POKéMON uses the bright part of its body, which changed from a dorsal fin, to lure prey."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Volt Absorb","hidden":false,"description":"If hit by an Electric-type move, the Pokémon has its HP restored instead of taking damage."},{"name":"Illuminate","hidden":false,"description":"By illuminating its surroundings, the Pokémon prevents its accuracy from being lowered."},{"name":"Water Absorb","hidden":true,"description":"If hit by a Water-type move, the Pokémon has its HP restored instead of taking damage."}],"eggGroups":["Water 2"],"genderRate":4,"hatchCounter":20,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"slow","habitat":"sea","color":"Blue","shape":"Fish","evolution":{"id":170,"name":"Chinchou","condition":null,"children":[{"id":171,"name":"Lanturn","condition":"Lv. 27","children":[]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[0,254],[0,255],[0,256],[1,48],[1,55],[1,86],[1,486],[1,598],[12,61],[16,109],[20,209],[24,268],[30,435],[36,392],[42,175],[48,36],[54,56]],"machine":[97,133,59,268,451,886,109,174,605,38,598,604,486,527,203,263,812,416,56,63,58,196,710,330,182,60,240,156,503,214,164,57,36,851,87,86,85,521,352,127,250,528],"egg":[54,60,487,389,352],"tutor":[]},"cards":[{"id":"sv7-49","name":"Lanturn","set":"Stellar Crown","date":"2024-09-13","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"49","artist":null,"img":"sv7/49"},{"id":"sv4pt5-21","name":"Lanturn","set":"Paldean Fates","date":"2024-01-26","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"21","artist":"aspara","img":"sv4pt5/21"},{"id":"swsh12-52","name":"Lanturn","set":"Silver Tempest","date":"2022-11-11","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"52","artist":"aoki","img":"swsh12/52"},{"id":"swsh7-53","name":"Lanturn","set":"Evolving Skies","date":"2021-08-27","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"53","artist":"ryoma uratsuka","img":"swsh7/53"},{"id":"swsh1-69","name":"Lanturn","set":"Sword & Shield","date":"2020-02-07","rarity":"Rare","number":"69","artist":"Naoyo Kimura","img":"swsh1/69"},{"id":"sm12-72","name":"Lanturn","set":"Cosmic Eclipse","date":"2019-11-01